{"paper": "2024-Tier1-10-Sep-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Find the values of x, y and z, so as to satisfy the equations given below: x + y + z = 12; x + y – z = 6; x – y + z = 4", "options": [{"text": "x = 5, y = 4, z = – 3", "added": false}, {"text": "x = 5, y = – 4, z = 3", "added": false}, {"text": "x = 5, y = 4, z = 3", "added": false}, {"text": "x = 5, y = – 4, z = – 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A policeman noticed a thief at a distance of 500 metres. The policeman started running and the thief also started running at the same time. The thief is running at a speed of 15 km/h. It took 15 minutes for the policeman to catch the thief. Find the speed of the policeman (in km/h).", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The given table shows the number of books on different subjects. What is the ratio of the number of books for subject B1 to the average number of books per subject?", "options": [{"text": "3 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "10 : 11", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "If A:B = 6 : 8 and B:C = 5 : 12, then A:B:C is:", "options": [{"text": "11:32:44", "added": false}, {"text": "10:23:14", "added": false}, {"text": "14:31:28", "added": false}, {"text": "15:20:48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "ΔEFG and ΔHIJ are similar. Also, ∠ E = ∠ H and ∠ F = ∠ I. If 3EF = HI and FG = 9 cm, then IJ is equal to ____.", "options": [{"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "27 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Study the given bar-graph and answer the question that follows. The bar-graph shows the sales of books (in thousands) from six branches (B1, B2, B3, B4, B5 and B6) of a publishing company during two consecutive years 2000 and 2001. The total sales of branch B6 for both the years is what percentage of the total sales of branch B3 for both the years (correct up to two decimal places)?", "options": [{"text": "70.69%", "added": false}, {"text": "73.17%", "added": false}, {"text": "69.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "82.26%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "Places A and B are 20 km apart on the highway. A car starts from A and another from B at the same time. If the cars travel in the same direction at different speeds, they meet in one hour. If they travelled towards each other, they met in 12 minutes. What are the speeds (in km/h) of two cars?", "options": [{"text": "60, 40", "added": false}, {"text": "52, 48", "added": false}, {"text": "51, 49", "added": false}, {"text": "55, 45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "If 45° and 65° are the angles of a triangle, then find the exterior angle of the third angle (remaining angle).", "options": [{"text": "110°", "added": false}, {"text": "120°", "added": false}, {"text": "70°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A right triangle with sides 3 cm, 4 cm and 5 cm is rotated about the sides of 3 cm to form a cone. The volume of the cone so formed is:", "options": [{"text": "20π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "16π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "25π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "28π cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Pipe L can fill a pool in 30 hours and pipe M in 45 hours. If both the pipes are opened in an empty pool, how much time will they take to fill it?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "47", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A merchant has 1000 kg of sugar, part of which he sells at a 10% profit and the rest at a 40% profit. He gains 20% on the whole. The quantity sold at 40% profit is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The concentrations of three acids, A, B, and C, are specified as 20%, 30%, and 40%, respectively. They are blended in a ratio of 3 : 5 : a, yielding a solution with a concentration of 30%. What is the value of 'a'?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "alligation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0.48", "added": false}, {"text": "0.28", "added": false}, {"text": "0.37", "added": false}, {"text": "0.42", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Ravi's salary was increased by 50%. After some time, his new salary was also increased by 50%. Find his gain percentage of salary.", "options": [{"text": "125%", "added": false}, {"text": "100%", "added": false}, {"text": "200%", "added": false}, {"text": "150%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The given bar graph shows the production of bikes by a company (in thousands) over the years. In how many of the given years was the production of bikes more than the average production of bikes over the years?.", "options": [{"text": "1 year", "added": false}, {"text": "2 years", "added": false}, {"text": "3 years", "added": false}, {"text": "4 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "If (7777+77) is divided by 78, then the remainder will be:", "options": [{"text": "76", "added": false}, {"text": "77", "added": false}, {"text": "78", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "Two successive discounts of 40% and 30% are equal to a single discount of:", "options": [{"text": "70%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}, {"text": "58%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "In a circle of radius 5√13 cm, a chord is at a distance of 10 cm from the centre of the circle. Find the length (in cm) of the chord.", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "What annual instalment will discharge a debt of ₹26,160 due in 4 years at 6% simple interest p.a.?", "options": [{"text": "₹4,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Simplify ​21 −[6 + 7 − {3.22 − (1.1 × 0.2)}].", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}]}